## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, Joe Biden explicitly and repeatedly stated during the 2020 presidential campaign and after taking office that "I am not banning fracking." His official policy position, as confirmed by his campaign and running mate, was to ban new oil and gas leasing on federal lands, not to impose a nationwide prohibition on fracking. No federal law or executive order has been issued to ban the practice entirely. The evidence directly contradicts the claim's assertion that Biden expressed a desire to ban fracking in the US.

